# Parallel fleet E2E

House, Budget, Kaizen, Language, and Health **run in parallel** — each on its own simulator and Metro port.

| Brand | Simulator | Metro | Scoped kill |
|-------|-----------|-------|-------------|
| house | House-A | :8083 | `scripts/e2e/maestro-scoped-kill.sh house` |
| budget | Budget-A | :8082 | `… maestro-scoped-kill.sh budget` |
| kaizen | Kaizen-A | :8081 | `… maestro-scoped-kill.sh kaizen` |
| language | Language-A | :8084 | `… maestro-scoped-kill.sh language` |
| health | Health-A | :8085 | `… maestro-scoped-kill.sh health` |

## Forbidden

Never run global Maestro cleanup:

```bash
# BAD — kills all five brands mid-run
pkill -9 -f 'maestro.cli|maestro-driver|run-house|run-budget|run-health|run-kaizen|run-language'
pkill -f 'maestro.cli.AppKt'
```

Never shut down other brands' simulators when resetting one brand.

## Allowed

- Preflight (sims + Metro + app install): `scripts/e2e/preflight-fleet-parallel.sh`
- Start all five suites: `scripts/e2e/run-fleet-parallel.sh` (preflights, then sets `E2E_PARALLEL_FLEET=1`, `E2E_DEDICATED_SIM=0`, `E2E_MAESTRO_LOCK=0` — each brand keeps its own sim + Metro + Maestro driver)
- Reset **one** brand: `scripts/e2e/maestro-scoped-kill.sh <brand>`
- `E2E_MAESTRO_CLEANUP=0` during runs (default in `setup-maestro-cleanup.sh`)
- Single-brand runs use exclusive sim mode (`E2E_DEDICATED_SIM=1` default) — shuts down other fleet sims

## Parallel fleet quick start

```bash
eval "$(./scripts/secrets/export-env.sh)"
npm run start:kaizen   -- --port 8081 &
npm run start:budget   -- --port 8082 &
npm run start:house    -- --port 8083 &
npm run start:language -- --port 8084 &
npm run start:health   -- --port 8085 &
./scripts/e2e/run-fleet-parallel.sh
```

Preflight auto-creates missing fleet iPhone sims when `E2E_AUTO_CREATE_SIM=1` (default). Set `E2E_PREFLIGHT_STRICT=0` to skip app-install checks.

## Agents

When retrying or priming a single brand, use that brand's scoped kill only. Do not wait for other brands to finish before starting House (or any) Maestro.
